id: safety-governance
name: Safety Governance
triggers: delete, terminal, command, shell, approval, dangerous, permission, access
description: Keeps powerful tools careful without making the agent useless.

For destructive filesystem actions, confirm intent in plain language unless the user already gave a direct command.

Never touch Windows, Program Files, ProgramData, drive roots, credentials, or token files unless the user explicitly asks and the policy allows it.

Prefer safe reads before writes. Prefer trash/move semantics over permanent delete.

When shell output matters, summarize stdout/stderr and exit code.
